cast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Alaska remains a Republican-leaning state in presidential politics, having backed the GOP nominee in every election since 1968, and its partisan lean sits roughly six points to the right of the nation. With the incumbent term-limited, the race is open, and no general-election polls or expert ratings have been published, so the forecast leans on fundamentals.\n\nRecent coverage highlights a favorable national climate for Democrats and treats Alaska as a possible future battleground, citing competitive downballot races and a potential Senate flip. Still, presidential results in the state have recently run well to the right of its underlying lean, and midterm-era Democratic momentum may not carry into a presidential contest. Republicans enter as modest favorites, with unusually wide uncertainty given the absence of polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2436, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3013, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2918, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3121, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2994, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.311, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2901, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2902, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2839, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2961, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2887, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3221, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.316, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3428, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2873, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3381, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2828, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2931, "margin": -5.5}, {"date":